>You re-enter the store/level/whatever.
>None of the 'good guys' know that this is your second time through,
>so...
>They are still after you.  
>
>Makes complete sense...no bug.

In particular, since (I presume) your old and new characters have the same
name, the shopkeeper considered them the same character.

"They say that shopkeepers can't tell identical twins apart."  (This is an
actual fortune cookie message.)

However, if your characters have different names, then the shopkeeper won't
be angry.  (However, the Kops still will go after you; after all, they're
Keystone Kops.)  The shopkeeper, instead of demanding that you pay, will
say, 

"Hi, <your new name>, I'm looking for <your old name>."

So, one solution to the bones problem is to rename your characters after
you get killed by a shopkeeper and leave a bone file.

